Give the seat the keyboard group's keyboard, not the device's

cage puts each keyboard in a group, and its key handlers hand the seat the group's keyboard,
but a new keyboard set the device itself as the seat's keyboard. Devices come and go: when
the session pauses (Couch switches the console to Kodi's tty2) libinput removes them, and
wlroots doesn't add them back until the next input arrives. Meanwhile the seat had no
keyboard, so a window that opened then got no keymap, and Chromium crashed on YouTube after
Plex. The group stays and keeps its keymap.

For Couch (https://github.com/alecschoen/couch), on top of Raspberry Pi OS's cage 0.3.1.

--- a/seat.c
+++ b/seat.c
@@ -414,7 +414,11 @@
 
 	cg_keyboard_group_add(keyboard, seat, virtual);
 
-	wlr_seat_set_keyboard(seat->seat, keyboard);
+	/* Couch: the seat gets the group's keyboard, as the key handlers already do, not the
+	   device's. A device goes away whenever the session pauses (another VT, Kodi), and
+	   the seat's keyboard with it: windows that open after that get no keymap, and
+	   Chromium crashes without one. The group stays, with its keymap. */
+	wlr_seat_set_keyboard(seat->seat, keyboard->group ? &keyboard->group->keyboard : keyboard);
 }
 
 static void
